//==
// # Face meshes
//
// Layer 05-face-meshing, second half: the criteria, the triangulation of a region in parameter
// space, the face mesh lifted to 3D, and the outcome a face meshing returns. Every UvCoordinate
// holds natural parameters (see uv-regions.types.plato).
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Criteria
//  - Triangulations in parameter space
//  - Face meshes in space
//  - Outcomes

//==
// # Criteria

// What a face mesh must achieve beyond its boundary.
//   Discretization: layer 04's edge criteria; they fix every boundary point.
//   SurfaceChordal: the largest distance, in model units, from a sample point of an element (the
//     midpoint of an element edge that is not a model-edge segment, or the corner mean) to the
//     surface (ElementDeviation).
//   SurfaceAngular: the largest angle between the face normals at the two ends of an element edge
//     that is not a model-edge segment: the normal turn across an element, as OpenCascade
//     AngleInterior and ACIS SPANORMALTOL define it (EdgeNormalTurn). The same value separately
//     bounds the angle between an element's normal and the face normal at its parameter centroid;
//     the turn does not imply that bound (a sliver can fold).
//   PreferQuads: emit a structured quad grid where QuadGridIfRectangular builds one.
type FaceMeshingCriteria
    implements IValue
{
    Discretization: DiscretizationCriteria;
    SurfaceChordal: Number;
    SurfaceAngular: Angle;
    PreferQuads: Boolean;
}

//==
// # Triangulations in parameter space

// A subdivision of a UvRegion into triangles and quads in natural parameters. Points[i] came
// from Sources[i]; elements index Points. The first BoundaryCount(region) points are the
// region's boundary points (outer loop, then each hole) unchanged; every later point is
// Interior. Every element is positively oriented in the face's chart (ElementChartArea > 0).
type UvTriangulation
    implements IValue
{
    Points: Array<UvCoordinate>;
    Sources: Array<UvPointSource>;
    Triangles: Array<TriangleFace>;
    Quads: Array<QuadFace>;
}

//==
// # Face meshes in space

// One face meshed. Parameter-space points and 3D vertices are distinct index spaces:
//   UvPoints, Sources, LocalVertex, Normals: one entry per parameter-space point, the points of
//     the UvTriangulation it was lifted from, in the same order.
//   LocalVertex[i]: the local 3D vertex of parameter-space point i; the copies of a seam point
//     and the points of one pole segment share one.
//   Positions, Provenance: one entry per local 3D vertex.
//   Normals[i]: the face normal at UvPoints[i] (the surface normal times the face's sense); at a
//     point on a collapsed line (a pole or an apex), the limit along its parameter line (layer
//     01's LimitNormal).
//   Triangles, Quads: elements over parameter-space point indices, counter-clockwise about the
//     face normal in 3D; elements that collapse at a pole are dropped or reduced (Lift).
type FaceMesh
    implements IValue
{
    Face: BrepFaceIndex;
    UvPoints: Array<UvCoordinate>;
    Sources: Array<UvPointSource>;
    LocalVertex: Array<VertexIndex>;
    Positions: Array<Point3D>;
    Normals: Array<Direction3D>;
    Triangles: Array<TriangleFace>;
    Quads: Array<QuadFace>;
    Provenance: Array<MeshVertexProvenance>;
}

//==
// # Outcomes

// What QuadGridIfRectangular found for a region.
//   NoGrid: the region is not four-sided, or a quad could not be kept for a reason a count
//     change cannot fix; the face gets triangles.
//   CountsDiffer: four-sided, but opposite sides have different segment counts; Floors gives,
//     per edge (indexed by BrepEdgeIndex, 0 for none), the segment count that would match. The
//     face gets triangles this round.
//   Grid: the structured grid, every quad planar and convex, failing quads split.
type QuadGridOutcome
    = NoGrid
    | CountsDiffer(Floors: SegmentFloors)
    | Grid(Mesh: UvTriangulation);

// The result of meshing one face. A blocking request (IsBlocking: a loop that is not simple in
// parameter space) comes with an empty mesh; an advisory request (a segment too coarse in
// parameter space, a quad count mismatch) comes with a valid triangle mesh. Every request has a
// diagnostic.
type FaceMeshOutcome
    implements IValue
{
    Mesh: FaceMesh;
    Requests: Array<EdgeRefinementRequest>;
    Diagnostics: Array<Diagnostic>;
}
